course: dictionary
lesson: 2338
title: Crunch: sound, sums and sit-ups
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Crunch» can be a doing word (a verb), a naming word (a noun), or both. The words around it show you which one. «Poppy hugs her new bunny and announces, "Snowy's getting a carrot every single day"» and then she says Bugs Bunny has watched rabbits «crunching them for years». Crunching carrots means biting them hard so they make a crisp, cracking sound.
explain: «Tasmanian devils are the biggest meat-eating marsupials alive; their strong jaws crunch whole carcasses, bones and fur included.» Here crunch is a verb. Try the swap: "their strong jaws bite whole carcasses, bones and fur included" still makes sense, so crunch means bite and press hard.
explain: Crunch can also be a noun: «the crunch of snow or leaves» is the loud sound itself. Crunches with an s can mean sit-ups for your stomach muscles. And «crunch numbers» means do a lot of sums, so this word also works in maths.
fact: Crunch (verb) means to bite or press something hard so it makes a loud cracking sound.
fact: A crunch (noun) is that loud cracking sound, like the crunch of leaves under your feet.
fact: Crunches (plural) are exercises, like sit-ups, that work the stomach muscles.
fact: To crunch numbers means to do a lot of sums.
fact: «Parrotfish crunch coral with their beaks», and this is one way fine sand is made on tropical beaches.
exercise: «Tasmanian devils' strong jaws crunch whole carcasses.» What does crunch mean here? | To sing loudly at night | To be sad and very tired | To hide quietly under a rock | *To bite and press hard, so bones make a cracking sound
exercise: Dad says, "Do ten crunches before bed." What are crunches? | Sums you do in your head | *Sit-ups for the stomach muscles | Crisp, juicy apples | A loud cracking sound
exercise: Sam hears the crunch of frost under her boots. What is a crunch here? | Doing lots of sums | *The loud cracking sound | A type of boot | An exercise for the legs
test: «Our teacher wants us to crunch numbers before lunch.» What does crunch numbers mean? | To make a loud cracking sound | *To do a lot of sums | To bite the numbers | To count the crunches in the gym
test: «The parrotfish crunches coral with its beak.» Which word means the same as crunches here? | hides from | smiles at | *bites hard | sings to
exam: Which sentence uses crunch as a noun? | We crunch apples every morning | Ella crunches the paper into a ball | *The crunch of the snow under our boots was loud | She will crunch the numbers tonight
